nning for no deal circumstances  because it wasn't going to happen  because he had a deal ready to go he  said he had a deal not labor  let's see that deal let's get it over  the line and let's all move on together  mr reed whilst we have you we really  should dwell on uncovered 19 and of  course christmas is very much in  all of our minds at the moment i i just  wonder whether or not  you feel that it would be wrong to relax  uh  restrictions for that five day christmas  uh period  given the numbers that we are seeing  from various parts of the country  including london  in terms of infection  well you know people have had a very  difficult year  nine months where people haven't been  able to go to work properly see their  families properly  people are looking forward to christmas  it's not going to be a normal christmas  of course  and the the rise that we're seeing well  the reported rise in infection rates  in many areas under tier 2 actually is  half of them it's not just london it's  very very  worrying now we'll get an assessment  based on the data on the 16th  of this month and we'll need to see  where we are then but the key thing is  we need to follow the science  and we need to do everything we can to  keep people safe so  the situation will be under review until  we understand from the science  what is driving the increase in  infection rates and what can be done to  manage that i mean the key thing is all  of us need to do whatever we can to  follow the rules and the guidelines  to stop the infection rate growing but  until we understand what's causing that  it's very difficult to say what we  should do as a result of that but  we should be only days away from finding  that out we should indeed uh steve reed  lovely to see you this morning merry  christmas when it comes  merry christmas thank you
 

